# Teach site — no class-materials claims

Public teach pages must **never** say or imply that we possess, mirror, or give out university lecture notes, slides, past papers, assignment packs, or other course materials.

## Hard bans (public copy)

Do not write variants of:

- EN: "Private materials show…", "Evidence from the course folder…", "we have the lecture notes / slides / past papers", "full course pack", "download the notes"
- CN: "现有材料里能看到…", "从课程材料看…", "其余讲义微信联系", "领取完整课件/讲义", "我们有课件/笔记/past paper"

Internal paths under `teaching/` and admin hints that materials are private are fine. Do not surface that inventory on indexed pages.

## Allowed

- Ask the **student** to send **their** brief, PDF, code, or screenshot of **their** lecture slide when booking.
- Show **our** tutoring decks / sample slides, clearly framed as tutoring content we wrote (not the university’s notes).
- Name syllabus topics in plain language without claiming we hold the official files.

## Sample slides / FAQ

- OK: "Sample slides from our probability tutoring deck are below."
- Not OK: "We have the class notes / 其余讲义微信索取."
- CTA: book tutoring on WeChat — do not promise a course-material dump.

## Generators

`enrich_teach_courses.py` and `teach_pages.rb` must not emit materials-inventory claims into `lead_*` / `overview_*` / FAQ.

## Covered topics chips

Public `topics` must be syllabus concepts in plain language (theme pack / lexicon).

Never publish:

- `Week N: <folder or file basename>` chips
- Raw lecture/worksheet/slide filenames (`lecture02`, `AY25…Tutorial+Worksheet`, `…canvas`, course-code-only labels)
- Quoted private assessment filenames in `stuck` / `tutoring` / meta

If private materials are scanned for evidence, use them only to pick theme / lexicon hits — never as the chip text.
